WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:02.040
Look out, Sony.

00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:05.180
Hawkeye is taking aim at you — and he never
misses.

00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:10.140
On August 20, Hollywood was rocked when reports
surfaced that Sony and Disney couldn't come

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:14.700
to terms on a new agreement to keep Tom Holland's
Spider-Man in the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:16.140
"Thank you, Mr. Stark.

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:17.800
But I'm...

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:18.320
I'm good."

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:20.400
"You're good?

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:21.760
How are you good?"

00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:27.210
Unless the circumstances change dramatically,
it looks like the 23-year-old Holland is done

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:32.740
showing up in MCU movies after five appearances
over the past three years, beginning with

00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:38.120
2016's Captain America: Civil War and ending
with 2019's Spider-Man: Far From Home.

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:43.550
The vast majority of people involved — including
Marvel Studios head Kevin Feige and Holland

00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:48.560
himself — have kept quiet so far on the
bombshell news, but one of the Avengers has

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:49.560
spoken out.

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:54.680
Jeremy Renner has played Clint Barton, also
known as Hawkeye, in the MCU for eight years

00:00:54.680 --> 00:01:00.240
since first appearing in 2011's Thor, took
to Instagram on August 21 to vent his feelings

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:01.780
on the controversial subject.

00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:05.840
He uploaded a still of himself in Avengers:
Endgame with a caption that reads,

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:11.300
"Hey @sonypictures we want Spider-Man back
to @therealstanlee and @marvel please, thank

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:16.380
you #congrats #spidermanrocks #🏹#please."

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:22.080
Poor grammar and odd hashtagging aside, it's
clear that Renner is clamoring for a new Spidey

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:24.980
deal, and that he falls on the Disney side
of the dividing line.

00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:29.980
Renner has many irons in the fire — including
starring in major Hollywood films, launching

00:01:29.990 --> 00:01:34.820
a musical career, and appearing in some slightly
strange Jeep commercials — but it's obvious

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:37.980
that Disney and Marvel offer the actor his
steadiest gig.

00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:41.840
The man knows how hard it can be to find work
in Hollywood, having been a makeup artist

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:46.420
early in his career to make ends meet at a
time where he couldn't find casting anywhere.

00:01:46.420 --> 00:01:51.620
Thankfully, Renner's place in the MCU is locked
tight, as he's slated to star on the upcoming

00:01:51.620 --> 00:01:55.760
Marvel series Hawkeye set for release on the
Disney+ streaming service sometime

00:01:55.760 --> 00:01:56.600
in the future.

00:01:56.600 --> 00:02:01.060
Some might say it's smart of Renner to not
look a gift horse in the mouth and instead

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:04.960
come to Disney's defense after Sony has put
the blame on the House of Mouse.

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:09.500
But it's also possible that he just really
likes the new Spider-Man movies, and doesn't

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:13.500
want to deal with a disaster like The Amazing
Spider-Man 2 again.

00:02:13.780 --> 00:02:16.520
"Too bad about that Spider-Guy.

00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:19.080
Too bad he's disappeared.

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:20.480
Seems like everybody really needs him."

00:02:20.580 --> 00:02:25.220
After the events of Avengers: Endgame and
Spider-Man: Far From Home, the web-slinger

00:02:25.220 --> 00:02:30.420
seemed poised to take on a central role in
the MCU by continuing Tony Stark's legacy

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:32.620
and keeping the memory of his late mentor
alive.

00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:37.200
Unfortunately, placing Peter Parker at the
center of the MCU may have been a misstep

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:42.200
on the part of Marvel's Feige, as it arguably
puts Disney at a distinct disadvantage in

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:43.690
negotiations with Sony.

00:02:43.690 --> 00:02:49.440
With Sony having the sole film rights to Spider-Man
— rights the company has held since 1999,

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:54.209
when Marvel was holding a licensing fire sale
to stave off bankruptcy — Disney was already

00:02:54.209 --> 00:02:56.700
on the wrong side of the corporate power-struggle.

00:02:56.700 --> 00:03:01.080
Setting Spider-Man up to become an Avenger
and a key cog in the future of the franchise

00:03:01.090 --> 00:03:03.160
may have only made matters worse.

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:07.400
Now they've set up a story that may well be
unfinished, depending on how things shake

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:08.280
out.

00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:12.740
Hopefully Renner's plea for help is the first
of many public comments by Marvel-related

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:18.010
figures on the Marvel-Sony split; after all,
this is the social media age where everyone

00:03:18.010 --> 00:03:20.940
and their mother lets loose their every thought
online.

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:25.480
The major players have been decidedly quiet
on the subject thus far, though fans are surely

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:29.000
waiting with bated breath to hear what Tom
Holland himself has to say.

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:33.240
It would also be very interesting to hear
what Marvel head honcho Feige has to say after

00:03:33.250 --> 00:03:37.840
having Spider-Man ripped from his future MCU
plans after righting the ship for Sony in

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:38.800
the first place.

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:42.660
For now, Marvelites will have to be happy
with Hawkeye taking his aim and shooting his

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:43.660
shot.

